cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "predykt: a toolkit for rigorous feature interaction analysis in machine learning"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Salem
    given-names: Hisham
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-07-31"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HishamSalem/predykt"
url: "https://github.com/HishamSalem/predykt#readme"
abstract: >-
  predykt is a Python toolkit for feature interaction analysis in tabular
  machine learning. It provides cyclical optimal binning, SHAP interaction
  testing against a simulated additive null, cross-algorithm voting, residual
  representation testing, and seed robustness validation, organised as a
  layered protocol in which each layer removes a different way a result can be
  an artifact of one arbitrary choice.
keywords:
  - machine-learning
  - feature-engineering
  - shap
  - feature-interactions
  - credit-risk
  - weight-of-evidence
  - optimal-binning
  - model-validation
